<urn:atm:triage:finding/RSH-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RSH-002" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "reconcile_peer delivery loop fails fast on transport error with no partial-success tracking, causing duplicate redelivery on retry" ;
  triage:description "In crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs, reconcile_peer/sync_peer's delivery loop (~lines 638-700) aborts on first transport error without recording which messages in the batch were already successfully delivered. A subsequent retried sync re-transmits already-delivered messages, compounding with the related missing rate-limit/watermark gap (AI24-IMPORTANT-002). Found by rust-service-hardening-agent during AICH-S4-FIX-2 recheck at 6d8ee8c3 on feature/pAI-s24-host-qualified-ack-receipt. Recommended to triage alongside AI24-IMPORTANT-002 since a watermark fix likely resolves both." ;
  triage:category "reliability" ;
  triage:severity "Minor" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "invalid" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-25T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-27T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "2026-07-27 (quality-mgr): superseding the 2026-07-27 correctionNote below with a real closure. On 2026-07-27 I retracted a prior waiver claim because ADR-038 is Status:Proposed and cannot settle architecture. arch-ctm subsequently pointed to docs/requirements.md REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-003/003A/003B, which I independently read (lines 3819-3960) and confirm ARE current, authoritative (non-Proposed) requirements, not a draft ADR: REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-003 states 'no replay store, outbox, retry queue, deferred receipt, remote acknowledgement state, or duplicate-delivery subsystem may exist' and 'duplicate arrival is idempotent at storage by the existing message ULID'; REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-003B states the drain lease 'contains no message ID, payload, cursor, receipt, or attempt history' and 'the lower bound is dropped with the in-memory lease and is never durable state.' This means the absence of cross-call partial-success tracking this finding flags is not an omission -- it is an explicitly mandated design constraint; adding it would violate REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-003B. Separately, the cited code no longer exists in the form described: crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/peer_sync.rs (with its delivered_request_json set) has been fully replaced by crates/atm-daemon/src/peer_drain_coordinator.rs::PeerDrainCoordinator::drain(), a page-based rewrite with a transient (created_at, message_ulid) lower bound that is dropped on lease release/failure, matching REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-003B exactly. Closing as invalid: the described behavior is required architecture, independently confirmed against current authoritative requirements docs and current code, not merely asserted by arch-ctm." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RSH-002/pAI-s21pre/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RSH-002/pAI-s22/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RSH-002/pAI-s23/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RSH-002/pAI-s24/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RSH-002/integrate-8750587b> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RSH-002/pAI-s27/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s27/35cb19f8> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s27/35cb19f8> .

